  {
    "id": "anno-izuhara_upper_p019_left-04",
    "type": "Annotation",
    "body": [
      {
        "purpose": "transcribing",
        "value": "合／錢貳萬七千六百七拾九貫九百四拾八文／金ニシテ貳千七百六拾七兩九合九勺四才"
      },
      {
        "purpose": "modern_jp_reading",
        "value": "合 錢 二万七千六百七十九貫九百四十八文／金にして 二千七百六十七兩九合九勺四才"
      },
      {
        "purpose": "english_translation",
        "value": "Total copper cash: 27,679 kan 948 mon; reckoned in gold, 2,767.994 ryo. The single 合 heads a double-column gloss whose right run gives the cash sum and left run its gold equivalent; the two agree at exactly ten kan to the ryo (27,679.948 divided by 10 = 2,767.9948, the printed figure truncating the last place). After 兩 the glyphs 合/勺/才 are tenths, hundredths and thousandths of a ryo, not koku sub-units."
      },
      {
        "purpose": "identifying",
        "value": "合錢"
      }
    ],
